"The <strong>Histogram</strong> graph shows the timings at the present setup: a histogram, the normal curve with the same mean and standard deviation, the number within ±s and ±2s of the mean, and a normal quantile plot below it. The Analysis section in the sidebar gives n, the mean period, s and s/√n under <strong>This setup</strong>, then <strong>The shape of these timings</strong>: the counts within ±s and ±2s, the correlation r of the quantile plot, and the mean ḡ and standard deviation s_g of g = {#}π²L/T² worked out from each timing.",
